BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261008T230000Z
DTEND:20261009T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20261008T000000Z
SUMMARY:Banned Together: A Banned Books Week Film Screening & Panel Discussion
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a film screening of this 2025 award-winning 
 documentary\, which "follows three students and their adult allies as they 
 fight to reinstate 97 books suddenly pulled from their school libraries. As 
 they evolve from local to national activists - meeting with bestselling 
 authors\, politicians\, Constitutional experts\, and more\, the film 
 reveals the dark forces behind the accelerating wave of book bans in the 
 U.S." The film will be followed by a discussion with Dorothy Yaun '27 and 
 Kate Selvitelli '30\, moderated by Dr. Shireen Campbell.
LOCATION:Hance Auditorium
CATEGORIES:Banned Books Week, Special Event
UID:LibCal-7393-17709049
URL:https://davidson.libcal.com/event/17709049
END:VEVENT
